    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0923" n="911" xml:id="pg911"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.51/7–146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-03T20:00:00-04:00">July 3, 1946—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>492. 1. Embstels 719 and 720, July 1.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d716-f1"/> No
                    foundation for AP despatch re $100 million loan.
                    Despatch apparently result irresponsible misinterpretation of interview with
                    Dept.</p>
                <p>2. With approval National Advisory Council, Eximbank approved today participation up to $25 million in exporter
                    credits for Turkey. Total amount of exports this credit will finance depends on
                    private credits which may be advanced by exporters or private banks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
